{"t":"2026-05-28T03:38:52.808Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141orb53GF4kFpvCxUEPe19","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n     2→# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n     3→\n     4→\"\"\"\n     5→Auto-seed the first admin user on startup.\n     6→\n     7→Creates Sean Young (Space Cowboy #9) as the default admin if no users exist.\n     8→This lets you skip manual account creation during MVP development.\n     9→\"\"\"\n    10→\n    11→from sqlalchemy import select, func\n    12→from sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\n    13→\n    14→from backend.database import AsyncSessionLocal\n    15→from backend.models.auth import User\n    16→from backend.logging_config import logger\n    17→\n    18→\n    19→SEED_EMAIL = \"spy@seanyoung.biz\"\n    20→SEED_NAME = \"Sean Young\"\n    21→\n    22→\n    23→async def seed_admin_user() -> None:\n    24→    \"\"\"Create the default admin user if the users table is empty.\"\"\"\n    25→    async with AsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n    26→        # Only seed if no users exist at all\n    27→        result = await session.execute(select(func.count()).select_from(User))\n    28→        user_count = result.scalar_one()\n    29→\n    30→        if user_count > 0:\n    31→            logger.info(\"seed.skip\", reason=\"users already exist\", count=user_count)\n    32→            return\n    33→\n    34→        admin = User(\n    35→            email=SEED_EMAIL,\n    36→            name=SEED_NAME,\n    37→            is_active=True,\n    38→            is_onboarded=False,  # Will go through onboarding to upload resume\n    39→        )\n    40→        session.add(admin)\n    41→        await session.commit()\n    42→\n    43→        logger.info(\n    44→            \"seed.admin_created\",\n    45→            email=SEED_EMAIL,\n    46→            name=SEED_NAME,\n    47→            user_id=str(admin.id),\n    48→        )\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b31d414-b90c-4812-8da6-f7c04cc82e58","uuid":"94f53ec8-e6a9-438f-b70f-a02a516bc5f3","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/backend/seed.py","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\n\"\"\"\nAuto-seed the first admin user on startup.\n\nCreates Sean Young (Space Cowboy #9) as the default admin if no users exist.\nThis lets you skip manual account creation during MVP development.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom sqlalchemy import select, func\nfrom sqlalchemy.ext.asyncio import AsyncSession\n\nfrom backend.database import AsyncSessionLocal\nfrom backend.models.auth import User\nfrom backend.logging_config import logger\n\n\nSEED_EMAIL = \"spy@seanyoung.biz\"\nSEED_NAME = \"Sean Young\"\n\n\nasync def seed_admin_user() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create the default admin user if the users table is empty.\"\"\"\n    async with AsyncSessionLocal() as session:\n        # Only seed if no users exist at all\n        result = await session.execute(select(func.count()).select_from(User))\n        user_count = result.scalar_one()\n\n        if user_count > 0:\n            logger.info(\"seed.skip\", reason=\"users already exist\", count=user_count)\n            return\n\n        admin = User(\n            email=SEED_EMAIL,\n            name=SEED_NAME,\n            is_active=True,\n            is_onboarded=False,  # Will go through onboarding to upload resume\n        )\n        session.add(admin)\n        await session.commit()\n\n        logger.info(\n            \"seed.admin_created\",\n            email=SEED_EMAIL,\n            name=SEED_NAME,\n            user_id=str(admin.id),\n        )\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:38:58.809Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01GsVwqwj1Scd3SbK88uarhi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context I need. Let me create the seeder.py file. According to the HYPHA spec:\n- `synthetics/fixtures/seeder.py` — idempotent loader that upserts synthetic candidates into Postgres on backend boot\n- Uses UUIDv5 for deterministic IDs: `uuid.uuid5(uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS, \"synthetic-\" + slug)`\n- Should read candidates from `candidates.yaml` (created by sibling agent)\n- Must be idempotent — no duplicates on repeated runs\n\nLet me create the directory structure and the seeder:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":70421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":731,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b31d414-b90c-4812-8da6-f7c04cc82e58","uuid":"afebed2a-5500-4988-8ade-e50adea2917b"}}
