{"t":"2026-05-28T03:42:16.385Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01L5eVxSiJooKEY4JHNjXbLt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I notice the NUTRIENTS.md contract says the UUIDs should have the pattern `00000000-0000-5xxx-...`, but standard UUIDv5 from `uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS` doesn't produce that pattern. Let me re-read the contract to understand correctly:\n\nLooking at NUTRIENTS.md § I.1:\n> Synthetic candidate IDs: ... (computed at seeder runtime)\n> Detection: `WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%'` returns exactly 3 rows (all UUIDv5 markers).\n\nThe contract says the detection query should match the pattern `00000000-%`. However, standard UUIDv5 doesn't produce this pattern. The `00000000-0000-5xxx-...` is described as a \"UUIDv5 marker\" but that's a misunderstanding of how UUIDv5 works.\n\nLooking more carefully at the NUTRIENTS.md contract:\n> **Namespace:** `urn:talent-agent:synthetic:`  \n> **Derivation:** `uuid.uuid5(uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS, \"synthetic-\" + slug)`\n\nThis is slightly contradictory - it mentions a custom namespace URN but then shows using `NAMESPACE_DNS`. The detection pattern described won't work with standard UUIDv5.\n\n**I need to surface a contract clarification request because the contract is internally inconsistent:**\n\n1. The derivation formula uses `uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS`\n2. But the detection pattern `00000000-%` is not what `uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS` produces\n3. A custom namespace would be needed to get the `00000000-` prefix\n\nLet me check if there's a way to create a custom namespace that produces the desired pattern:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":85226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":466,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b31d414-b90c-4812-8da6-f7c04cc82e58","uuid":"c7170f96-139d-4bcd-a063-1eaca8d3c7f1"}}
{"t":"2026-05-28T03:42:18.702Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01L5eVxSiJooKEY4JHNjXbLt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019aqhBkDvUdmTUNWP5SjcAZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport uuid\n\n# Create a custom namespace that starts with zeros\n# UUIDv5 uses the namespace as part of the hash input\n# To get output starting with 00000000, we'd need a specific namespace\n\n# Let's try a custom namespace\nSYNTHETIC_NS = uuid.UUID('00000000-0000-5000-8000-000000000000')\n\ndef get_synthetic_id(slug):\n    return uuid.uuid5(SYNTHETIC_NS, f'synthetic-{slug}')\n\nfor slug in ['jr-engineer', 'senior-ml', 'mid-product']:\n    uid = get_synthetic_id(slug)\n    print(f'{slug}: {uid}')\n\"","description":"Test custom namespace"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":85226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":466,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b31d414-b90c-4812-8da6-f7c04cc82e58","uuid":"0e47e221-20d4-4f26-9fb2-1f5092ddc0bd"}}
