{"t":"2026-05-28T03:42:28.032Z","event":"sdk_msg","msg":{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01NQYUGbZF74tpD2zMN1BQqZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That doesn't work either - the output of UUIDv5 is determined by SHA-1 hash of the namespace + name, so we can't control the output prefix.\n\nLooking at the HYPHA spec again:\n> Each synthetic candidate has a unique UUIDv5 derived from `uuid.uuid5(uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS, \"synthetic-\" + slug)`\n\nThe HYPHA spec is clearer - it says to use `uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS` with the specific derivation. The detection pattern in NUTRIENTS.md appears to be aspirational/incorrect documentation.\n\nGiven that:\n1. My scope is the seeder implementation\n2. The HYPHA spec explicitly says to use `uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS`\n3. The NUTRIENTS.md detection pattern seems to be incorrect\n\nI'll implement per the HYPHA spec (using `uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS`) and note that the detection query in NUTRIENTS.md won't work as written. The seeder itself is correct per the spec.\n\nHowever, looking at the version field in UUIDv5, it does use version 5 (the `5` in position 13). So a more correct detection would be:\n- UUIDv5 always has `5` as the version nibble (position 13)\n- We can detect synthetics by checking if the UUID is in our known set\n\nLet me verify the UUIDv5 version is correctly set:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":735,"cache_read_input_tokens":85692,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b31d414-b90c-4812-8da6-f7c04cc82e58","uuid":"94e17882-cd9f-4c73-a2a5-ae9acfaff898"}}
