st practices, trained 50+ engineers\n   148→\n   149→      Machine Learning Engineer | Uber ATG | Pittsburgh, PA | Aug 2016 - Dec 2018\n   150→      - Developed real-time object detection models for self-driving vehicles\n   151→      - Implemented distributed training infrastructure using Horovod across 128 GPUs\n   152→      - Built A/B testing framework for ML model deployment with statistical rigor\n   153→      - Published research on domain adaptation for weather-robust perception systems\n   154→\n   155→      Research Scientist Intern | Google Brain | Mountain View, CA | Summer 2015\n   156→      - Researched attention mechanisms for sequence-to-sequence models\n   157→      - Contributed to TensorFlow open-source project (2 merged PRs)\n   158→\n   159→      EDUCATION\n   160→\n   161→      Ph.D. in Computer Science (Machine Learning) | Carnegie Mellon University | 2016\n   162→      - Dissertation: \"Efficient Deep Learning for Resource-Constrained Environments\"\n   163→      - Advisor: Dr. Geoffrey Hinton (visiting), Dr. Ruslan Salakhutdinov\n   164→      - NSF Graduate Research Fellowship\n   165→\n   166→      M.S. in Computer Science | Stanford University | 2012\n   167→      - Focus: Artificial Intelligence and Natural Language Processing\n   168→\n   169→      B.Tech in Computer Science | IIT Bombay | 2010\n   170→      - Gold Medalist, Department of Computer Science\n   171→\n   172→      TECHNICAL SKILLS\n   173→\n   174→      Languages: Python, C++, CUDA, SQL, Rust (learning)\n   175→      ML Frameworks: PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, Hugging Face Transformers\n   176→      Infrastructure: Kubernetes, Ray, Spark, Airflow, MLflow, Weights & Biases\n   177→      Cloud: AWS (SageMaker, EKS, S3), GCP (Vertex AI, TPU), Azure ML\n   178→      Specializations: LLMs, RAG systems, distributed training, model optimization,\n   179→        computer vision, NLP, MLOps\n   180→\n   181→      PUBLICATIONS (Selected)\n   182→\n   183→      - \"Efficient Attention Me