 of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b31d414-b90c-4812-8da6-f7c04cc82e58","uuid":"3e1fca0b-5ede-47bb-bdfd-7c4dd8678588","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/spy/mfautomations/repos/creation-station/reverse-search/synthetics/fixtures/candidates.yaml","content":"# Copyright 2026 VibeSpace LLC\n# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n\n# Synthetic Candidate Fixtures for Drift Detection\n#\n# These 3 deterministic synthetic candidates exercise the Discovery -> Score\n# pipeline daily. Each candidate has a unique UUIDv5 derived from:\n#   uuid.uuid5(uuid.NAMESPACE_DNS, \"synthetic-{slug}\")\n#\n# The UUID marker pattern 00000000-0000-5xxx- allows detection via SQL:\n#   SELECT * FROM candidates WHERE id::text LIKE '00000000-%'\n#\n# Contract: NUTRIENTS.md I.1, I.9\n\ncandidates:\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  # SYNTHETIC-JR-ENGINEER\n  # Entry-level full-stack developer, 1-2 years experience\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - slug: synthetic-jr-engineer\n    name: Jordan Chen\n    email: jordan.chen.synthetic@talent-agent.test\n    linkedin_url: https://linkedin.com/in/synthetic-jr-engineer\n    github_url: https://github.com/synthetic-jr-engineer\n    identity_context:\n      location: New York, NY\n      target_salary_min: 80000\n      target_salary_max: 110000\n      remote_preference: hybrid\n      experience_years: 2\n      leadership_level: IC\n    target_locations:\n      - New York, NY\n      - Remote\n    excluded_companies:\n      - Palantir\n      - Meta\n    excluded_industries:\n      - Defense\n      - Gambling\n    resume_text: |\n      JORDAN CHEN\n      Full-Stack Software Engineer\n      New York, NY | jordan.chen@email.com | linkedin.com/in/jordanchen | github.com/jchen-dev\n\n      SUMMARY\n      Enthusiastic full-stack developer with 2 years of experience building modern web\n      applications. Passionate about clean code, user experience, and continuous learning.\n      Seeking opportunities to grow my skills while contributing to impactful products.\n\n      EXPERIENCE\n\n      Software Engineer | TechStart Inc. | New York, NY | June 2024 - Present\n      - Developed and maintained React-based dashboard serving 15,000+ daily active users\n      - Built RESTful APIs using Node.js and Express with PostgreSQL database integration\n      - Implemented automated testing suite achieving 85% code coverage with Jest and Cypress\n      - Collaborated with design team to improve UI/UX, reducing user support tickets by 30%\n      - Participated in Agile ceremonies including daily standups and sprint retrospectives\n\n      Junior Developer (Intern to Full-Time) | WebFlow Agency | Brooklyn, NY | Jan 2023 - May 2024\n      - Created responsive landing pages and marketing sites for 20+ small business clients\n      - Migrated legacy jQuery codebase to modern React, improving page load time by 40%\n      - Assisted senior developers in debugging production issues and optimizing database queries\n      - Wrote technical documentation for internal tools and onboarding processes\n\n      EDUCATION\n\n      Bachelor of Science in Computer Science | New York University | May 2023\n      - GPA: 3.6/4.0\n      - Relevant Coursework: Data Structures, Algorithms, Web Development, Database Systems\n      - Hackathon Winner: NYU HackNight 2022 - Built real-time collaborative note-taking app\n\n      TECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n      Languages: JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, HTML5, CSS3, SQL\n      Frontend: React, Next.js, Redux, Tailwind CSS, Material UI\n      Backend: Node.js, Express, FastAPI, REST APIs, GraphQL basics\n      Databases: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis\n      Tools: Git, GitHub, Docker basics, VS Code, Figma, Jira\n      Testing: Jest, React Testing Library, Cypress\n\n      PROJECTS\n\n      TaskFlow - Personal Project Management App (github.com/jchen-dev/taskflow)\n      - Built full-stack task management app with React frontend and Node.js backend\n      - Implemented real-time updates using WebSockets for collaborative features\n      - Deployed on Vercel (frontend) and Railway (backend) with CI/CD via GitHub Actions\n\n      WeatherNow - React Native Mobile App\n      - Developed cross-platform weather app using React Native and OpenWeatherMap API\n      - Implemented location-based weather with push notifications for severe weather alerts\n\n      CERTIFICATIONS\n      - AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner (2024)\n      - Meta Front-End Developer Professional Certificate (2023)\n\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  # SYNTHETIC-SENIOR-ML\n  # Staff-level ML engineer, 8+ years experience\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - slug: synthetic-senior-ml\n    name: Dr. Priya Ramanathan\n    email: priya.ramanathan.synthetic@talent-agent.test\n    linkedin_url: https://linkedin.com/in/synthetic-senior-ml\n    github_url: https://github.com/synthetic-senior-ml\n    identity_context:\n      location: San Francisco, CA\n      target_salary_min: 250000\n      target_salary_max: 350000\n      remote_preference: remote_only\n      experience_years: 9\n      leadership_level: Staff\n    target_locations:\n      - San Francisco, CA\n      - Remote\n    excluded_companies:\n      - Oracle\n      - IBM\n    excluded_industries:\n      - Oil and Gas\n      - Tobacco\n    resume_text: |\n      DR. PRIYA RAMANATHAN\n      Staff Machine Learning Engineer\n      San Francisco, CA | priya.ram@email.com | linkedin.com/in/priyaram | github.com/priya-ml\n\n      SUMMARY\n      Staff-level ML engineer with 9 years of experience building production ML systems at\n      scale. Expert in deep learning, distributed training, and MLOps infrastructure.\n      Published researcher with 12 peer-reviewed papers. Proven track record of leading\n      cross-functional teams and delivering ML products used by millions of users.\n\n      EXPERIENCE\n\n      Staff Machine Learning Engineer | Anthropic | San Francisco, CA | March 2022 - Present\n      - Lead technical direction for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) infrastructure\n      - Architected distributed training pipeline processing 500TB+ of text data monthly\n      - Reduced model inference latency by 60% through quantization and caching optimizations\n      - Mentored team of 6 ML engineers, establishing best practices for experiment tracking\n      - Collaborated with research team on novel attention mechanisms for long-context models\n\n      Senior Machine Learning Engineer | Scale AI | San Francisco, CA | Jan 2019 - Feb 2022\n      - Built data labeling quality assurance system using active learning, improving label\n        accuracy from 92% to 98.5%\n      - Designed and deployed computer vision pipeline for autonomous vehicle annotation\n      - Led migration from TensorFlow 1.x to PyTorch, reducing training time by 35%\n      - Authored internal course on MLOps best practices, trained 50+ engineers\n\n      Machine Learning Engineer | Uber ATG | Pittsburgh, PA | Aug 2016 - Dec 2018\n      - Developed real-time object detection models for self-driving vehicles\n      - Implemented distributed training infrastructure using Horovod across 128 GPUs\n      - Built A/B testing framework for ML model deployment with statistical rigor\n      - Published research on domain adaptation for weather-robust perception systems\n\n      Research Scientist Intern | Google Brain | Mountain View, CA | Summer 2015\n      - Researched attention mechanisms for sequence-to-sequence models\n      - Contributed to TensorFlow open-source project (2 merged PRs)\n\n      EDUCATION\n\n      Ph.D. in Computer Science (Machine Learning) | Carnegie Mellon University | 2016\n      - Dissertation: \"Efficient Deep Learning for Resource-Constrained Environments\"\n      - Advisor: Dr. Geoffrey Hinton (visiting), Dr. Ruslan Salakhutdinov\n      - NSF Graduate Research Fellowship\n\n      M.S. in Computer Science | Stanford University | 2012\n      - Focus: Artificial Intelligence and Natural Language Processing\n\n      B.Tech in Computer Science | IIT Bombay | 2010\n      - Gold Medalist, Department of Computer Science\n\n      TECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n      Languages: Python, C++, CUDA, SQL, Rust (learning)\n      ML Frameworks: PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, Hugging Face Transformers\n      Infrastructure: Kubernetes, Ray, Spark, Airflow, MLflow, Weights & Biases\n      Cloud: AWS (SageMaker, EKS, S3), GCP (Vertex AI, TPU), Azure ML\n      Specializations: LLMs, RAG systems, distributed training, model optimization,\n        computer vision, NLP, MLOps\n\n      PUBLICATIONS (Selected)\n\n      - \"Efficient Attention Mechanisms for Long-Context Language Models\" - NeurIPS 2023\n      - \"Domain Adaptation for Robust Perception in Adverse Weather\" - CVPR 2018\n      - \"Active Learning for Data-Efficient Model Training\" - ICML 2020\n      - 9 additional peer-reviewed publications (Google Scholar: 2,400+ citations)\n\n      PATENTS\n      - US Patent 11,234,567: \"Method for Efficient Inference in Transformer Models\"\n      - US Patent 10,987,654: \"System for Automated ML Pipeline Orchestration\"\n\n      SPEAKING\n      - NeurIPS 2023: Workshop on Efficient Deep Learning\n      - PyTorch Conference 2022: Distributed Training at Scale\n      - MLOps Community Summit 2021: Building Reliable ML Systems\n\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  # SYNTHETIC-MID-PRODUCT\n  # Senior product manager, 5 years experience\n  # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - slug: synthetic-mid-product\n